1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,273
On the very day he was named
the best player in Europe…

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:05,690
his relationship with Barça's coach
fell apart.

3
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:09,590
And the best player in the world…
found himself on the bench.

4
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:13,740
But believe me…
that wasn't the hardest thing he faced.

5
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:16,863
Because before Barcelona…
before the Ballon d'Or…

6
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:20,040
this boy grew up
poorer than you can imagine.

7
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:25,340
Malnutrition left his body weak,
and he lost several teeth as a child.

8
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:28,490
He walked long distances
just to get to training…

9
00:00:28,630 --> 00:00:31,910
because, simply put,
he couldn't afford the bus fare.

10
00:00:32,130 --> 00:00:35,900
That boy's name was…
Rivaldo Vítor Borba Ferreira.

11
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:39,383
Born in 1972 in Recife,

12
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:43,040
in north-east Brazil,
into a very poor family.

13
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:47,260
But one person believed
his son could become a great player…

14
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,020
his father, Romildo.

15
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,153
He encouraged him,
followed him,

16
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:52,520
and dreamed with him.

17
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:56,540
But in 1989…
tragedy struck.

18
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:59,400
Rivaldo's father died in an accident.

19
00:00:59,500 --> 00:01:01,930
And Rivaldo decided to quit football.

20
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:03,910
For him, the dream was over.

21
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:05,463
But his mother refused.

22
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:06,690
She said: keep going…

23
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:09,360
because it was the dream
his father believed in.

24
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:10,730
And Rivaldo kept going.

25
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:12,263
He started at Santa Cruz,

26
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:15,003
then Mogi Mirim,
then Corinthians,

27
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:18,800
and Palmeiras…
until Europe started to notice him.

28
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,233
1996…

29
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:24,740
Rivaldo arrived in Spain
through Deportivo La Coruña.

30
00:01:24,890 --> 00:01:26,413
And one season was all it took…

31
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:29,250
for Barcelona
to decide they wanted him.

32
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:31,663
Summer 1997…

33
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:34,153
Barcelona had just lost
Ronaldo Nazário,

34
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:35,930
who had moved to Inter Milan.

35
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,773
The club needed
a new Brazilian star.

36
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,200
And the choice fell on Rivaldo.

37
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:49,740
And that's where…
the key chapter of his story began.

38
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:54,193
In his first two seasons at Barcelona…
Rivaldo won La Liga twice,

39
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,770
and the Copa del Rey once.

40
00:01:55,910 --> 00:02:01,600
But what happened in 1999…
officially put him on top of the world.

41
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:05,310
21 December 1999.

42
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:07,710
The Ballon d'Or winner is announced.

43
00:02:07,910 --> 00:02:10,583
David Beckham was coming off
a historic season,

44
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:13,390
having won the treble
with Manchester United.

45
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,120
But the result was…

46
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,950
Beckham: 154 points.

47
00:02:19,050 --> 00:02:21,463
Rivaldo: 219.

48
00:02:21,530 --> 00:02:24,440
Rivaldo wins the Ballon d'Or.

49
00:02:24,530 --> 00:02:30,590
And he also wins FIFA's
World Player of the Year for 1999.

50
00:02:30,770 --> 00:02:33,643
The boy who struggled
just to get to training…

51
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:35,760
became the best player in the world.

52
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:38,423
It should have been
his happiest time…

53
00:02:38,490 --> 00:02:39,200
Right?

54
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:40,880
No.

55
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:43,093
Because with the Ballon d'Or…

56
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:46,630
came one of the strangest crises
of Rivaldo's time at Barcelona.

57
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:49,710
Louis van Gaal wanted him
on the left wing.

58
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,923
Rivaldo felt his best position
was through the middle…

59
00:02:52,990 --> 00:02:54,540
behind the strikers.

60
00:02:54,710 --> 00:02:55,923
The dispute grew…

61
00:02:55,990 --> 00:02:59,480
and Rivaldo said he no longer wanted
to play on the wing.

62
00:02:59,590 --> 00:03:01,260
Van Gaal answered in his own way.

63
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:04,420
He dropped the best player in the world
from the team.

64
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:08,590
The Ballon d'Or in his hands…
and his place in the side not guaranteed.

65
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:14,670
But if you want to know
what kind of player Rivaldo was…

66
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:17,280
you only need to watch one night.

67
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,793
17 June 2001.

68
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:21,920
The final matchday of La Liga.

69
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,080
Barcelona v Valencia…
at the Camp Nou.

70
00:03:25,230 --> 00:03:28,243
The maths was simple:
Barcelona had to win…

71
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:30,510
to qualify for the Champions League.

72
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:34,913
And Rivaldo produced one
of his greatest games for Barcelona.

73
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:36,113
The first goal…

74
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:37,693
a direct free kick.

75
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:38,643
1-0.

76
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:40,100
Valencia equalise.

77
00:03:40,210 --> 00:03:42,003
Rivaldo gets the ball far out…

78
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:42,963
and shoots.

79
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:43,933
A second goal.

80
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,023
2-1.

81
00:03:45,090 --> 00:03:46,930
Valencia equalise again.

82
00:03:47,050 --> 00:03:48,103
2-2.

83
00:03:48,170 --> 00:03:49,543
And time is running out.

84
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:50,573
With that score…

85
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,913
Barcelona are out of the Champions League.

86
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:54,353
The 87th minute.

87
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:57,123
Frank de Boer sends the ball
towards the box.

88
00:03:57,190 --> 00:03:58,653
Rivaldo takes it on his chest…

89
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,043
the ball still in the air…

90
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:01,750
he throws himself backwards…

91
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:03,303
a bicycle kick.

92
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:04,710
Goal.

93
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:07,083
3-2.

94
00:04:07,150 --> 00:04:08,293
A hat-trick for Rivaldo.

95
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:10,993
Barcelona are in the Champions League.

96
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:12,803
The Camp Nou erupted.

97
00:04:12,870 --> 00:04:16,403
And in a single moment…
Rivaldo saved Barcelona's season…

98
00:04:16,470 --> 00:04:19,490
with one of the most famous goals
in the club's history.

99
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:23,340
But his story still
needed one final scene.

100
00:04:23,510 --> 00:04:24,893
Summer 2002.

101
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:28,403
Rivaldo lines up with Brazil
in the World Cup final.

102
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:30,363
Brazil against Germany.

103
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:34,550
Brazil win 2-0…
and Rivaldo becomes a world champion.

104
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,633
But back from the World Cup…

105
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:39,570
he found Van Gaal back
in charge of Barcelona.

106
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:41,710
And Rivaldo decided to leave.

107
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:44,573
From a child who knew poverty and hunger…

108
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:47,723
who lost his father
while just starting out…

109
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:50,093
to a player who held the Ballon d'Or…

110
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:55,923
who scored an impossible goal to save
Barcelona on one of its biggest nights…

111
00:04:55,990 --> 00:05:00,540
and then lifted the World Cup
wearing Brazil's No. 10.

112
00:05:00,830 --> 00:05:02,670
That was the story of…

113
00:05:03,150 --> 00:05:04,253
Rivaldo.

114
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:08,350
One of the greatest Brazilians
ever to wear the Barcelona shirt.

115
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:09,613
In the next episode…

116
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:13,903
we'll talk about another Brazilian who
joined Barça a year after Rivaldo left.

117
00:05:13,970 --> 00:05:17,880
But this time…
the smile was part of the game.

118
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:19,370
Ronaldinho.

